module gunbc.ci_gate

data self_host_fixed_point_gate_retirement_note: String = "THREE GATES RETIRED WITH THE REGEN LOOP (v1 cut). RegenVerifyGate ran `regen_stage0 --verify`; SelfHostStalenessGate and SelfHostReadsRealBytesGate were the two halves of the realized-comparison receipt, which re-emitted the stage0 sources into target/v2-emit-fresh-realize and compared them byte-wise against the committed src/v1/stage0/src. All three had ONE subject: the self-host fixed point -- does re-running the emitter over the v1 .dag authority reproduce the committed seed. The v1 cut deleted that authority and the regen binary, so there is nothing to re-emit and nothing to compare; the question is not unanswered, it is no longer a question. RECEIPT that this retirement was forced rather than chosen for convenience: CI run 31900396249 refused with `regen_verify_gate_passes detail=returned Bool(false) | regen-verify gate failed: regen_stage0 witness binary unavailable` -- the typed refusal the first cut commit predicted, fired. Retired, not narrowed: no gate was dispositioned out of an enrolled roster to get green, and the merge-admission surface loses the rows rather than keeping them with a skip arm.

WHAT DOES NOT RETIRE WITH THEM, stated so it is not read as wider than it is: the seed's Rust still compiles and the frozen .rs are still committed, so a fresh clone still builds gunbc. What is gone is the PROOF that those bytes are what the emitter would produce, because the emitter that produced them no longer exists to ask. Any future fixed-point claim belongs to v2's emitter as forward work and gets its own gate.\n\nAND THE MODEL LAYER SURVIVES, EXECUTING, which this note previously left a reader to infer wrongly from 'it is no longer a question'. That sentence is true of the LIVE comparison only. v2.compiler.self_host still carries canonical_emitted_bytes_digest, self_host_fixpoint_equal, fixed_point_scaffold, regen_staleness_authority and their siblings, and v2.test.execution.self_host_fixed_point still runs 15 witnesses over them, measured green post-cut, INCLUDING the perturbation RED controls (digests diverge on perturbed regen source, scaffold violates on perturbed, validate rejects perturbed bytes). So what retired is the gate that asked the question OF THE LIVE SEED using a binary that no longer exists; what remains is the modeled fixed-point relation and its discriminating evidence, which is what a future v2-emitter gate would bind to rather than re-author. Distinguishing the two matters because a reader deciding whether to rebuild this later needs to know the model is already there and already has teeth."


type Gate
  = EmitHostGate
  | CheapClaimPoolGate
  | ExtdepsExternalAuthorityGate
  | DagCompileCleanGate
  | GeneratedArtifactDriftGate
  | ExtdepsScopePlacementGate
  | ProseRowIntroductionGate
  | SourceRootIngestGate
